    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the access point at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the access drive so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Keep the full width of the driveway clear of parked vehicles to allow emergency vehicles to reach the residence.\n• Create a designated turnaround area near the residence or detached structure so fire and emergency vehicles can reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Mark any low-clearance branches along the access drive that may obstruct tall emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back dense vegetation near the detached structure so responders can access all sides of that building.\n• Keep a clear path along the walkway connecting the residence to the parking and access areas so responders can move on foot without obstruction.\n• Post the property address visibly at both the road entrance and near the residence itself so responders can confirm they have reached the correct structure.\n• Coordinate with your local fire department to walk the property and identify any staging areas suitable for a second responding unit, given the single access point and limited turnaround space."
  },
