    "recommendations": "• Remove woody debris visible near the structure before fire season.\n• Thin scattered trees to create more open space between tree canopy and the roofline.\n• Trim shrubs that are close to the structure so bare ground separates them from the exterior walls.\n• Cut back mixed vegetation where it grows closest to the structure.\n• Mow or cut grass cover around the structure and near the driveway regularly during dry months.\n• Clear brush areas closest to the structure, working outward to reduce the amount of plants that could carry fire toward the building.\n• Keep the single access route clear of overhanging branches and low-hanging vegetation so emergency vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from within the brush areas nearest to the structure."
